  "question": {
    "text": "Consider the reversible isothermal expansion of an ideal gas in a closed system at two different temperatures <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> . The correct graphical depiction of the dependence of work done <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">w</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;vs&nbsp;the final volume <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mfenced></math> is:",
